WEBVTT

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:14.910
"Samurai's Back" "Aragaki's Back"
"1st in Qualifiers" "Will he win!?"
"Samurai's Real Strength" "Aragaki shows his stuff!"

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:16.540
"Samurai's Back" "Aragaki's Back"
"1st in Qualifiers" "Will he win!?"
"Samurai's Real Strength" "Aragaki shows his stuff!"

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:16.540
At yesterday's All-Japan,

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:20.120
Jotaro Aragaki showed us
a wonderful come-back performance.

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.540
Will he bring another Samurai wave?
We're looking forward to it.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:25.450
I'm going then.

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:27.790
Okay. I'll be there later.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:48.410
You should just smile.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:53.660
What? Seriously?

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:57.000
Leo said that's why he can't watch Dad compete.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:02.750
London, huh? So Leo-chi's
going back to his own battlefield.

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:06.910
Yeah, it's sad, but if
he says he wants to dance,

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:09.660
then we should send him off.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:13.370
It was weird that he was being
a ninja in Zoshigaya, huh?

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:16.330
No, I don't think so.

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:19.910
I mean, he became your family ninja because

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:22.540
he loved the Samurai's gymnastics
and wanted to see it, right?

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:24.410
It's not weird at all.

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:26.700
Isn't it weirder that he'd go home suddenly?

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:29.540
B-But he said it's so he can go back to ballet--

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:32.000
That's definitely not true!

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.750
He would've said something earlier if it were!

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:35.000
It's totally a lie.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.370
Huh...?

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:39.910
Hm... He could be right.

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:42.370
--Huh?
--Yeah, like definitely possible, maybe.

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:43.830
Huh?!

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:56.160
I was wrong!

00:01:58.330 --> 00:01:59.700
--Sending me to South America?!

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:01.250
--Sorry, Kazu. Please get out.
--Sending me to South America?!

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:02.120
Huh?

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:03.750
A bird who brings good luck.

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:04.660
Me?

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:07.410
Go to the venue first and tell Dad

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:09.910
that I'll definitely bring Leo!

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:10.950
Huh?

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:13.580
Oh, then take a message for me, too.

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:14.580
Huh?!

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:17.450
Hey, wait. How am I supposed to get there?

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:19.450
All right!

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:21.580
<i>I </i>will take you.

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:24.040
--Huh?!
--Thanks!

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:26.040
Kazu, I'm counting on you!

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.580
R-Right.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:29.750
Please.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.750
O-Okay!

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:35.250
Now, let's go.

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:37.950
"57th Annual All-Japan
Artistic Gymnastics Championships"
"November 14-16, 2003"

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:41.250
Was Rei happy?

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:43.370
Yeah. She was...

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:45.790
Hm? She's coming today, too, right?

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:48.040
She is, yeah.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:50.580
Daughters can be hard.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:55.790
Someday, she'll grow up.
And stop replying to your messages.

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:57.000
Seriously...?

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.200
Yeah, seriously.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:01.370
I told my daughter there'd be
a live broadcast today, too.

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:04.290
A lot can change in one year, you know.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:07.830
You and I were like that, too, though.

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:09.830
Thank you very much.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:24.660
He's completely different from yesterday.

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:27.870
Hurry, Grandma!

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:31.000
The agent said they would
leave the hotel just past noon.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:34.250
Isn't a round trip to and from Narita
gonna be cutting it super close?

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:36.870
That's why we need to hurry!

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:38.500
Quiet down!

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:40.580
"To Narita Airport"

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:47.500
Oh, there he is! Samura--
I mean, Aragaki's dad...

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:52.910
And now, we'll introduce the gymnasts.
Jotaro Aragaki, from Yotsuba Sports Club.

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:55.370
Aragaki's dad!

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:59.910
A-Aragaki... Aragaki's...

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:00.790
Huh?

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:05.750
Jotaro...!

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.540
Huh?

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:14.540
--Brit...
--It's Bri!

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:17.040
Come on, hurry.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:18.620
I have a message from Aragaki!

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:21.160
She said she'll bring Leo!

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:32.700
Also, Miss Ayu said
to tell Takizawa "Do your best!"

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:33.790
Love!

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:41.160
This is taking too long!

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:44.700
Grandma, can't you pass the car in front of us?

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:46.330
That's an unmarked police car.

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:47.160
What?!

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:48.450
Calm down.

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:51.370
You've heard the saying,
"Haste makes waste," right?

00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:58.330
Yes?

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:00.120
Where are you now?

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:03.120
As planned, we will arrive
at the airport shortly.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:04.580
We'll be there soon, too!

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:06.410
Please stall Leo!

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:09.200
Very well. Goodbye.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:10.580
Who was that?

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:13.290
Headquarters. Just checking in.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:22.040
Now, can Aragaki stick the landing?

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:26.580
He did it!

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:29.160
Aragaki stuck the landing solidly!

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:31.160
He's doing really well today, too.

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:34.080
He had a dynamic routine
that took advantage of his height.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:37.750
"Floor"

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:40.120
"Floor"

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:40.120
9.525!

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:43.200
Aragaki scores over 9.5!

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:45.830
His performance deserved that score.

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:48.660
Now, last up in Group 1 is Minamino.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:51.120
He made a lot of mistakes yesterday.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:52.870
I'm sure he wants to do better today.

00:05:56.910 --> 00:06:00.330
Oh? He's not wearing his usual arm covers today.

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:03.160
Perhaps it's a sign that he's moved on?

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:11.450
A double double layout!

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:13.790
He's landed a Super E level skill!

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:15.160
There was no hesitation.

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:17.950
He's completely dispelled
the bad impression from yesterday.

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:21.080
In addition, he had more twists
than Aragaki's Tsukahara.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:25.450
I can feel his strong will coming
through with that double double.

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:26.910
A Fedorchenko.

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:29.370
Front splits.

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:31.040
And finally...

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:38.830
He did it! A double double!

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:41.040
Wow, this really surprised me.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:42.830
He perfectly executed a routine

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:44.910
that would be considered
difficult at the world level.

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:45.830
"Floor"

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:48.160
"Floor"

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:48.160
9.775!

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:50.580
He's passed Aragaki!

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:54.200
This is Minamino! Tetsuo Minamino!

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:55.290
He's strong...

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:57.910
He won't let you win so easily, huh?

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:13.120
We're here.

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:16.000
Th-Thanks, Grandma...

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.950
Bring him back, even if you have
to pull him by the scruff of his neck.

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:21.040
Right! Let's go, Bigbird!

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:22.410
Me?

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:36.410
What's wrong?

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:37.700
There are people...

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:47.870
What are you doing?

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:49.160
There are people...

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:53.910
We can go through this.

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:55.080
Let's wait.

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:55.950
No...

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:58.120
Let's wait.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:07:59.450
We're waiting.

00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:11.620
Sorry 'bout that.

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:13.870
--It's a bird!
--Mr. Birdie!

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:18.120
No...!

00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:21.410
Sorry, Bigbird!

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:30.950
Found him!

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:35.790
What do you want?

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:41.410
Rei, go on ahead.

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:43.540
I'll take care of him!

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:45.000
Huh? But--

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:47.750
Don't worry about it. Just hurry up and go!

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:49.290
R-Right.

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:53.620
I haven't exercised much lately,

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:55.410
so this is perfect.

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:19.160
Here I go!

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:21.830
Bigbird?!

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:31.370
BB?!

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:32.540
Leo!

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:37.540
Rachel...

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:41.700
What are you trying to do?

00:09:54.450 --> 00:09:56.620
What are you doing here?

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:59.290
I think you should come
watch Dad compete after all.

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:00.620
We talked about that yesterda--

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:02.200
You're lying, Leo!

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:03.450
What are you talking about?

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:05.950
You're not saying "indeed"!

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:08.540
--That's--
--Forget about "this" or "that"!

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:11.120
I'm definitely taking you see Dad.

00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:13.870
If we don't hurry, the competition will be over!

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:15.830
I'm not going.

00:10:15.830 --> 00:10:18.080
Why not? Dad's waiting for you.

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:21.950
Joe can fight even if I'm not there!

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:25.200
Because unlike me, Joe's strong...

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:28.410
He's always so strong...

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:32.700
In the first place, Tomoyo is
a little different from what you think.

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:40.040
Dad's not always strong.

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:42.540
He's not a superhero from a movie.

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:48.000
He hasn't done well at gymnastics
ever since Mom died.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:51.080
He kept losing...

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:55.410
If you hadn't come, I think
he would've quit gymnastics.

00:10:55.410 --> 00:11:00.750
And even today, if you don't come,
Dad might lose again!

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:04.080
Please! Watch Dad's gymnastics to the end!

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:06.330
You're the Aragaki family ninja, aren't you?

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:08.500
The Samurai's in trouble!

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:11.000
You don't know anything, Rachel.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:15.910
I don't have the power to help Joe.

00:11:15.910 --> 00:11:19.120
Everything you said was a coincidence.

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:24.450
Even now, I got scared of Joe's
expectations and tried to run away.

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:27.250
I've just been running away this whole time!

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:29.580
If you knew the real me,

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:32.370
then you'd all be disappointed and go away!

00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:37.250
I'm here, aren't I?

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:38.580
Dad, too.

00:11:38.580 --> 00:11:43.080
If you're broken, then we'll stay with
you until you're not broken anymore!

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:44.870
We'll go to London, or wherever!

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:46.330
Because you're you!

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:50.660
Dad and I both want the you
that's here right now to watch!

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:55.040
"The way of the ninja is

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:56.830
to fight with your all to live!

00:11:56.830 --> 00:11:58.500
Only if you are prepared to die

00:11:58.500 --> 00:12:01.160
is there a path to life!

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:04.910
Knowing your weakness is like having
an unmoving blade in your heart,

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:07.830
opening the path of the ninja!

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:10.200
This predicament we find ourselves in

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:15.540
is an opportunity to acquire a steadfast heart,
without fear, contempt, or worry!

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:18.410
Those with the fortitude to bring about peace--

00:12:18.410 --> 00:12:22.370
If you want to become true ninjas,

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:25.830
then stand together with me now."

00:12:29.750 --> 00:12:32.370
Ooku vs. Kunoichi...

00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:41.160
Let's go together, Leo!

00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:44.500
"57th Annual All-Japan
Artistic Gymnastics Championships"
"November 14-16, 2003"

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:45.910
"57th Annual All-Japan
Artistic Gymnastics Championships"

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:45.910
Aragaki is about to start his turn for
the first group's fourth event, the vault.

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:48.160
Aragaki is about to start his turn for
the first group's fourth event, the vault.

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:49.200
"1. Tetsuo Minamino" "2. Jotaro Aragaki"
"3. Jun Dojima" "4. Shigeru Nishikiori"

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:52.120
"1. Tetsuo Minamino" "2. Jotaro Aragaki"
"3. Jun Dojima" "4. Shigeru Nishikiori"

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:52.120
In the still rings before this, Aragaki
scored 0.2 points more than Minamino,

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:54.790
"1. Tetsuo Minamino" "2. Jotaro Aragaki"
"3. Jun Dojima" "4. Shigeru Nishikiori"

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:54.790
slightly narrowing the gap between them.

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:57.160
Will he gain more on Minamino here?

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:05.250
Another Yeo II, like in the qualifiers!

00:13:06.250 --> 00:13:07.910
A slight stumble!

00:13:07.910 --> 00:13:11.160
The execution was very precise,
so it's disappointing!

00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:12.410
"Vault"

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:14.040
"Vault"

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:14.040
9.675!

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:17.040
"Vault"

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:17.040
It's definitely not a low score,
but the misstep here hurts.

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:24.500
He landed the Lu Yufu!

00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:27.370
Minamino lands beautifully here, too!

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:31.700
I've never seen a Japanese gymnast try
a Lu Yufu in an official competition before.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:33.040
Now, for the score.

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:36.540
"Vault"

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:36.540
9.725! A very high score!

00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:39.750
He's widened the gap between
him and Aragaki again!

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:42.580
Tetsuo Minamino is too strong!

00:13:42.580 --> 00:13:44.870
Aragaki needs to overtake him
in the remaining two events,

00:13:44.870 --> 00:13:47.950
the parallel bars and the horizontal bar.

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:53.620
Shoot... Is Leo-chi gonna make it?

00:13:53.620 --> 00:13:56.200
What're you doin'?

00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:57.370
Bigbird!

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:00.660
Grandma!

00:14:00.660 --> 00:14:02.450
Leave it to me.

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:11.620
--Y-Y-Y-You're going too fast and furious...!
--N-N-No...!

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:13.580
Woo-hoo!

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:18.580
Group 1 has finished the parallel bars.

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:21.700
With this, each group has
finished their fifth event.

00:14:21.700 --> 00:14:23.830
Let's take a look at the standings.

00:14:23.830 --> 00:14:26.660
"1. Tetsuo Minamino" "2. Jotaro Aragaki"
"3. Tomoki Takizawa" "4. Hiroshi Okamachi"
"5. Jun Dojima" "6. Shigeru Nishikiori"

00:14:23.830 --> 00:14:26.660
At the top right now is Tetsuo Minamino.

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:29.290
"1. Tetsuo Minamino" "2. Jotaro Aragaki"
"3. Tomoki Takizawa" "4. Hiroshi Okamachi"
"5. Jun Dojima" "6. Shigeru Nishikiori"

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:29.290
He scored high on the parallel bars, as well,

00:14:29.290 --> 00:14:31.830
"1. Tetsuo Minamino" "2. Jotaro Aragaki"
"3. Tomoki Takizawa" "4. Hiroshi Okamachi"
"5. Jun Dojima" "6. Shigeru Nishikiori"

00:14:29.290 --> 00:14:31.830
to give him a total of 47.425 points.

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:32.450
"1. Tetsuo Minamino"
"2. Jotaro Aragaki"
"3. Tomoki Takizawa"

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:35.410
"1. Tetsuo Minamino"
"2. Jotaro Aragaki"
"3. Tomoki Takizawa"

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:35.410
Next, still in second place, is Jotaro Aragaki.

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:38.000
"1. Tetsuo Minamino"
"2. Jotaro Aragaki"
"3. Tomoki Takizawa"

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:38.000
His total is 47.325.

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:42.700
"1. Tetsuo Minamino"
"2. Jotaro Aragaki"

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:42.700
The difference between him
and Minamino is 0.1 points.

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:46.290
Next, in third place is
Tomoki Takizawa. His total...

00:14:46.290 --> 00:14:47.830
Does it hurt?

00:14:47.830 --> 00:14:49.830
I'm fine.

00:14:49.830 --> 00:14:51.410
All right, done.

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:53.160
Thank you very much.

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:54.700
Sure.

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:56.000
Hm?

00:14:56.000 --> 00:15:02.950
I'm here right now because you agreed
to continue coaching me back then.

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:08.540
You idiot. Go win this.

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:10.040
Yes, sir!

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:14.250
Tecchan, I'm going to tell
you honestly what I think.

00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:18.000
No one can beat this Tetsuo Minamino right now.

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:19.870
Today's your day.

00:15:20.870 --> 00:15:22.540
I know.

00:15:24.120 --> 00:15:27.250
Now, Group 1 is on its
final event, the horizonal bar.

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:30.160
Starting them off is Minamino,
currently in first place.

00:15:33.290 --> 00:15:35.330
Now, Minamino starts here...

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:37.370
...with a Kolman...

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:42.200
...into a layout Tkatchev!

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:43.790
A Tkatchev!

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:45.450
A piked Tkatchev!

00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:46.870
And a Gienger！

00:15:46.870 --> 00:15:50.330
He executed four difficult
release skills in a row!

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:52.910
Is he a monster...?

00:16:00.540 --> 00:16:02.620
All that's left for Minamino is the landing!

00:16:05.410 --> 00:16:07.500
A layout double double!

00:16:09.040 --> 00:16:10.870
And he does it!

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:14.330
A great landing!

00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:16.500
I can't believe it.

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:21.000
Of course, the consecutive release skills
Minamino showed us had high point values,

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:24.830
but the risk of failure is also very high.

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:28.750
To do them without hesitation requires
not only world-class technique

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:31.870
but also extraordinary mental fortitude.

00:16:31.870 --> 00:16:37.080
He really is the gymnast most suitable
to carry the future of Japanese gymnastics.

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:39.040
Now, for his score...

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:42.580
"Horizonal Bar"

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:42.580
9.850! 9.850!

00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:44.040
--Yes!
--Minamino pulled out an unbelievable score!

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:46.450
--Minamino pulled out an unbelievable score!

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:52.540
"57th Annual All-Japan
Artistic Gymnastics Championships"

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:58.080
Are you worried about Jotaro?

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:02.410
Huh? Well, I was thinking about
how I could get better.

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:04.330
Including Takizawa, the three at the top

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:06.910
all feel like they do
whatever they want, you know?

00:17:06.910 --> 00:17:10.160
I thought maybe that was the secret.

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:12.950
You feel the same as them, though.

00:17:12.950 --> 00:17:14.910
Huh?

00:17:14.910 --> 00:17:17.580
It's almost Jotaro's turn.

00:17:17.580 --> 00:17:19.580
I wonder what'll happen...

00:17:39.080 --> 00:17:40.330
Dad!

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:08.330
Samurai!

00:18:08.330 --> 00:18:09.910
Last is Aragaki.

00:18:09.910 --> 00:18:14.250
In order to beat Minamino,
he needs at least a 9.95.

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:20.660
Amakusa?

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:22.330
R-Right.

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:41.450
He did it! The Aragaki!

00:18:54.330 --> 00:18:55.330
Wha--?!

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:03.120
Grab it!

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:04.370
I'll grab it!

00:19:07.910 --> 00:19:10.120
A piked Aragaki!

00:19:28.870 --> 00:19:32.000
H-He did it! A quadruple!

00:19:36.410 --> 00:19:37.910
A quadruple dismount!

00:19:37.910 --> 00:19:40.450
He successfully did a quadruple!

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:44.160
This is without a doubt the first time
this incredible feat has been performed!

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:51.160
Now, for his score!

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:54.500
"Horizontal Bar"

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:54.500
9.975! He got 9.975!

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:55.830
--Aragaki's won! Aragaki's won!

00:19:55.830 --> 00:19:57.500
--He did it!
--Aragaki's won! Aragaki's won!

00:19:57.500 --> 00:20:01.200
He drove off Minamino to win the glory!

00:20:03.750 --> 00:20:08.120
With the current rules,
the highest skill difficulty is Super E,

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:11.200
so difficulty can only add 0.3 points at most.

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:14.910
But the piked Aragaki he showed us

00:20:14.910 --> 00:20:18.950
and the quadruple dismount,
which may be called "Aragaki II"?

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:22.910
They both surpass the Super E
difficulty by a lot.

00:20:22.910 --> 00:20:25.500
There were much easier ways to get the points,

00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:28.500
but even so, he attempted them.

00:20:28.500 --> 00:20:32.330
I don't know how to express
how I feel right now.

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:37.370
What I do know is that his performance was
something that connected to the next era,

00:20:37.370 --> 00:20:38.500
without a doubt!

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:41.580
The Japanese gymnastics world
suffered for a long time,

00:20:41.580 --> 00:20:46.290
but is this competition a chance
to get out of that long, long tunnel?

00:20:46.290 --> 00:20:48.580
Japan's Samurai, Jotaro Aragaki.

00:20:48.580 --> 00:20:51.290
He showed the people of Japan--

00:20:51.290 --> 00:20:54.750
no, the people of the world--his way of living!

00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:57.250
"I saw on TV.
Not bad, Dad."

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:11.450
As expected of the only gymnast you admire.

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:53.200
He's fighting in an amazing place.

00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:56.410
I bet he never thought we'd come.

00:21:56.410 --> 00:21:59.330
No, I'm sure he knew we would.

00:22:10.660 --> 00:22:12.910
I'm sure of it.
